This group keeps its skills' `model:` pins on purpose.

Read by scripts/lint-frontmatter.py, which fails an active `model:` key
in any other group under skills/: VS Code's Claude session target reads
~/.claude/skills, and on a model from its Copilot group it can serve
only that group's models, so a pin can name one it cannot serve. Here
the pin is kept: `learn` pins `fable`, which the user kept on
2026-10-13, and should a `/learn` on a Copilot-routed model fail,
unpinning is one line.

The file's name is kept from the retired Copilot payload, whose script
read it to leave the group out of every copy. The marker is a file
rather than a list in the linter so the exemption lives beside the
skills it covers. A new group opts in by adding this file; nothing else
needs editing.

Why this group. `skills/meta/` holds skills whose subject is the agent
configuration itself, rather than the user's code or repo, and each is
reached by typing its name.
